; Leg BS -- the host RECEIVES.  The Victor sends RCVAG.DAT by name.
;
; NOTE THE DIRECTION.  This is the only leg in the sheet where the host is
; the receiver, so START THIS BEFORE typing STEPBS on the Victor -- the
; Victor is the initiator here and will give up if nothing answers its S
; packets.
;
; TWO RESULTS FOR ONE LEG:
;
;   1. It closes upstream edit 16, which shipped unverified.  A 16-bit rc at
;      ckuusy.c:3690 threw away zchki()'s return, which on success is the
;      FILE SIZE, so "-s <name>" refused any file of 32,768 through 65,535
;      bytes, periodically, every 64K.  The fixture is exactly 32,768
;      inside the broken range -- so a pass is meaningful and a failure is
;      diagnostic.  THE TELL for the old bug is "kermit -s NAME:" with an
;      EMPTY message after the colon: nothing set errno, because nothing
;      failed.  zchki() had succeeded and the caller threw the answer away.
;
;   2. It is the port's first send-direction measurement of any kind.
;      V9K_PREFIXING and ckvictor.c's prefixing initializer govern
;      Victor->host only (SS16ae: ctlp[] is read by the packet BUILDERS),
;      and no leg has ever exercised them.
;
; READING IT, and both of these are traps:
;   - "wire=" in the Victor's .OUT divides rxbytes, so on a send leg it
;     reports the ACK STREAM over the whole elapsed time.  It is not the
;     send rate.  The host's statistics is the send rate.
;   - pktstat.py MISREADS send logs: its "longest packet" reads the one-byte
;     LEN field, which is 0 for long packets, and its S- count is the HOST
;     retransmitting.  Read s16ahBS.pkt by hand.
;
; If it fails, the workaround is a wildcard -- "-s RCVAG.*" reaches
; nzxpand() and routes around the bug entirely.  That is a diagnostic, not a
; fix: a wildcard passing while the name fails IS the confirmation.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16ahBS.pkt
receive gotbs.dat
statistics
